spec:
  grid: 8-13 rows x 8-13 cols, always square [observed]
  frame:
    corners: bg color (4 cells)
    sides: each of top/bottom/left/right is a distinct solid color, all 5 colors (bg + 4 sides) are unique
    thickness: 1 cell
  interior:
    moving_pixels: 8-19 pixels whose color matches one of the 4 side colors; 0-6 per side
    static_pixels: 0-9 pixels in 0-3 colors not matching bg or any side color
    density: 12-27% of interior cells are non-bg
  constraints:
    no_collision: each moving pixel's destination (1 step toward matching side) is either bg or another moving pixel that vacates
    chain_allowed: a moving pixel may land on another moving pixel if that pixel also moves away (same or different direction); chains of length 1-2 observed
    adjacent_stay: pixel already adjacent to its matching frame side stays put (destination would be the frame itself)
  transform: each interior pixel matching a side color shifts 1 cell toward that side; everything else unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. pick N=8-13, create NxN grid filled with bg color
    2. choose 5 distinct colors for bg, top, bottom, left, right; paint frame sides (corners = bg)
    3. build the OUTPUT interior — place 8-19 side-colored pixels and 0-9 static pixels at random interior positions; ensure low density (<27%)
    4. derive INPUT by shifting each side-colored pixel 1 step AWAY from its matching side (reverse the transform); if a pixel is adjacent to its matching side in the output, it stays (already at boundary in input too)
    5. validate: no destination collisions in the forward direction; each forward-move destination is bg or a co-moving cell
